---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../assets/ashmit-portrait.png';
---
<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="introduction">
      <div>
        <p class="affiliation">Computer Science · NYU Abu Dhabi</p>
        <h1>Ashmit Mukherjee</h1>
        <p>I build software for human–AI experiments, agent simulations, protein language models, and scientific data collection.</p>
        <div class="intro-links"><a href="mailto:asm8879@nyu.edu">asm8879@nyu.edu</a><a href="https://github.com/Ansester" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a></div>
      </div>
      <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Ashmit Mukherjee" width={144} height={144} format="webp" loading="eager" />
    </header>

    <section class="home-section" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
      <h2 id="research-heading">Research</h2>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">Human–AI collaboration</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Research assistant with Ben Rosche and Hanan Salam · 2026–present</p>
        <p>I built the platform for experiments on AI advice and cooperation and lead its development. I connect Python game engines, adviser workflows, participant interfaces, and records that I can replay and check independently.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry" id="manuscript">
        <h3><a href="/work/protein-language-models/">Bio-LoRA and protein models</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Research assistant, eBRAIN Lab · Co-first author, unpublished manuscript</p>
        <p>I developed signal-peptide training and evaluation pipelines for protein language models. At 650M, BLOSUM62 feature injection reached 86.08% mean exact cleavage-site match across three seeds, compared with 83.64% for vanilla LoRA.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/biosynthesis-paper-database/">Biosynthesis paper database</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Research assistant, eBRAIN Lab · 2026–present</p>
        <p>I built an OpenAlex collection pipeline for the biosynthesis portion of a scientific-paper database. The November 2026 pull contains 139,011 raw records across three subdomains, with data cards and checks for coverage and topic mismatch.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="research-entry">
        <h3><a href="/work/synthetic-pilot-lab/">Synthetic Pilot Lab</a></h3>
        <p class="byline">Independent capstone · 2026–present</p>
        <p>I compare direct language-model forecasts with agent simulations against archived human experiments on punishment and cooperation. I built the benchmark and simulation tools to test whether interacting agents improve predictions enough to justify their extra computation.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="projects-heading">Other projects</h2><a href="/work/">All projects ↗</a></div>
      <p>I won the <a href="/work/csaw-llm-ctf/">CSAW 2026 LLM-CTF</a> with SegfaultObservers (Team MENA). I built a parallel agent workflow and per-challenge evidence records; my team recorded 22 flag recoveries across 23 challenges.</p>
      <p>I co-developed <a href="/work/roomwise/">RoomWise</a>, where you talk through furniture choices, swipe through listings, and see the room preview update with each selection. I also built <a href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens</a>, a local-model tool for querying incident records and inspecting the sources behind an answer.</p>
      <p>I’ve also worked on <a href="/work/hinglish-ner/">Hindi–English named-entity recognition</a>, <a href="/work/salary-regression/">salary regression</a>, and <a href="/work/camp/">a campus equipment app</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <h2 id="about-heading">A little background</h2>
      <div id="background">
        <p>I’m interested in computational social science, human–AI interaction, and the research methods needed to study them.</p>
        <p>I’m IT Head of the NYU Abu Dhabi Journal of Social Sciences, where I lead the journal’s technical work. I’m also part of the NYUAD Model United Nations Research Team and review conference background guides.</p>
        <p id="experience">I studied away at NYU Paris and NYU New York. At NYU Abu Dhabi, I’ve facilitated workshops for first-year students and worked front of house at the Arts Center. Previously, I was an <a href="/work/zeek/">ML engineering intern at Zeek</a>, working on customer segmentation and model comparison.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
